From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The LineageOS Project <noreply@lineageos.org>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] keymaster: disable CFI for libkeymaster3device

libkeymaster3device dispatches through the legacy keymaster 2.0 HAL ops table.
The stock MediaTek/Trustonic module (libMcTeeKeymaster.so) is not
CFI-instrumented, so Android 10 rejects the indirect call in
Keymaster2PassthroughContext::DeleteKey() and aborts the keymaster HAL during
fingerprint enrollment. That made keystore return a null credential response
and crashed Settings.

Follow the upstream AOSP fix for CFI failures in keymaster-adjacent binaries
("Turn off CFI for the Keymaster VTS", I12b145dad5535846d68c97954d31a93123bb95e7)
and build libkeymaster3device without CFI.
---
 Android.bp | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Android.bp b/Android.bp
index dae6f71..f2222af 100644
--- a/Android.bp
+++ b/Android.bp
@@ -236,6 +236,9 @@ cc_library_shared {
 cc_library_shared {
     name: "libkeymaster3device",
     vendor: true,
+    sanitize: {
+        cfi: false,
+    },
     srcs: [
         "legacy_support/keymaster_passthrough_key.cpp",
         "legacy_support/keymaster_passthrough_engine.cpp",
-- 
2.25.1
